    question: 'Which cloud storage is most secure?',
    answer: '<strong>Sync.com</strong> and <strong>pCloud</strong> offer zero-knowledge encryption, meaning even the provider cannot access your files. <strong>Dropbox</strong>, <strong>Google Drive</strong>, and <strong>OneDrive</strong> use encryption in transit and at rest but can technically access your files. For maximum security, choose a zero-knowledge provider. For enterprise compliance, all major providers offer SOC 2 and ISO certifications.'
