    question: 'Is cloud storage safe from hackers?',
    answer: 'Cloud storage is generally safe with proper precautions: <strong>Enable two-factor authentication (2FA)</strong>, use strong unique passwords, don\'t share sensitive files publicly, and enable zero-knowledge encryption if available (<strong>Sync.com</strong>, <strong>pCloud Crypto</strong>). Major providers like <strong>Google</strong>, <strong>Dropbox</strong>, and <strong>Microsoft</strong> have enterprise-grade security and rarely experience breaches. Most hacks result from weak user passwords, not provider vulnerabilities.'
