  <h2 id="collaboration-features">Collaboration Features Breakdown</h2>
  <p>If you work with a team, collaboration features are critical:</p>

  <h3>Real-Time Document Editing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Drive</strong> - Best-in-class with Google Docs, Sheets, Slides (free, unlimited)</li>
    <li><strong>OneDrive</strong> - Office Online works well, though Microsoft 365 subscription recommended</li>
    <li><strong>Dropbox</strong> - Dropbox Paper is decent but not as powerful as Google/Microsoft alternatives</li>
    <li><strong>Others</strong> - Most don't have native editing, rely on third-party integrations</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Commenting & Feedback</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Drive</strong> - Inline comments, suggestions, assign action items</li>
    <li><strong>Dropbox</strong> - Comment on files, @mention team members</li>
    <li><strong>Box</strong> - Advanced commenting with approval workflows</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>File Sharing Controls</h3>
  <p>All major providers offer:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Password-protected links</li>
    <li>Expiration dates on shared links</li>
    <li>View-only vs download vs edit permissions</li>
    <li>Ability to revoke access after sharing</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="security-encryption">Security & Encryption Comparison</h2>
  <p>Security is paramount when storing sensitive business data:</p>

  <h3>Encryption Standards</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Zero-knowledge encryption</strong> - Sync.com, pCloud Crypto, MEGA (even the provider can't access)</li>
    <li><strong>Encryption in transit & at rest</strong> - Google Drive, Dropbox, OneDrive, Box (provider has keys)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)</h3>
  <p>All major providers support 2FA. Always enable it for maximum security.</p>

  <h3>Compliance Certifications</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>SOC 2</strong> - Google, Microsoft, Dropbox, Box, Sync.com</li>
    <li><strong>HIPAA</strong> - Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Box, Dropbox Business</li>
    <li><strong>GDPR</strong> - All major providers</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="mobile-apps">Mobile App Experience</h2>
  <p>Mobile access is essential for remote workers on the go:</p>

  <h3>Best Mobile Apps</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Drive</strong> - Document scanning, offline access, automatic photo backup</li>
    <li><strong>Dropbox</strong> - Excellent document scanner, smooth offline mode</li>
    <li><strong>OneDrive</strong> - Good on iPhone, great on Windows Phone (RIP)</li>
    <li><strong>iCloud</strong> - Perfect on iOS, limited on Android</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Key Mobile Features</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Offline access</strong> - Download files for offline viewing/editing</li>
    <li><strong>Document scanning</strong> - Use phone camera to scan documents as PDFs</li>
    <li><strong>Photo backup</strong> - Automatically upload photos from camera roll</li>
    <li><strong>File management</strong> - Organize, rename, delete files on the go</li>
  </ul>

